Yes, thanks.

And I assume that you are using a binary version of Rgraphviz?

It is pretty standard that any graphviz problems don't occur until you  
actually do something like
R> example(layoutGraph)

What you see is somewhat typical of some problems with the R-Graphviz  
interaction. Unfortunately I am not that familiar with 64bit Vista  
(and frankly I have no interest in becoming familiar :)

Given that it does not work now, and that Graphviz seems to work  
separately, I would try to compile Rgraphviz from source. The hope is  
that doing this, might actually make everything work, or it might  
provide some clues as to what needs to be done. It may also be wasted  
work. But if you really want to get it to work, I would suggest  
spending 30 minutes compiling from source. I would be using the mingw  
version that the graphviz developer suggests, because it seems that  
the recommended version 2.20.3 does not work on Vista 64bit.  
Unfortunately, the graphviz developers tends to change the internals  
frequently, so it is not without reason that RGraphviz recommends a  
specific Graphviz version. In fact, what happens might be
   Graphviz 2.20.3 does not work on Vista 64 bit
   Rgraphviz does not work with the newer version
But this is all speculation.

Unless of course someone is actually experienced with the situation  
and can provide actual help instead of guesswork :)

Kasper

